-- title:
--   Torsion of J₀(N) over fields algebraic over 𝔽_ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime and let $K$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}/\ell$-algebra structure making it algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/\ell$; let $N$ be a nonzero natural number with $\ell \nmid N$. Write $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\ K\ N$ for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((X))$ over $K$ generated by the family $\mathrm{divisorExpansionsC}\ K\ N$ of $q$-expansions attached to level $N$, and let $\mathrm{JZeroC}\ K\ N$ be its degree-zero divisor class group, namely the quotient of the subgroup of degree-zero divisors of this field over $K$ by the subgroup of principal divisors intersected with it. The assertion is that every element $u$ of $\mathrm{JZeroC}\ K\ N$ has finite additive order; equivalently, there is an $m \ge 1$ with $m \cdot u = 0$. No finiteness is assumed of $K$ itself, only algebraicity over the prime field of characteristic $\ell$.
--
--   This is the statement that the points of the Jacobian $J_0(N)$ over a field algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_\ell$, realised as the degree-zero divisor class group of the level-$N$ modular function field in characteristic $\ell$, form a torsion group. It is used in the form [`ModularCurve.isOfFinAddOrder_jZeroC_residueField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isOfFinAddOrder_jZeroC_residueField), where the base is a residue field arising in the reduction of modular curves at primes away from the level.
